# Template for deploy/media.env (Joey TV WP-B1, Q23) - the guest container joey-media reads THIS file only.
# The real file lives ONLY on the NAS (/volume1/Docker/joey/life-dashboard/deploy/media.env, chmod 600, git- and
# docker-ignored). nas_scripts/media_env.sh builds it from deploy/.env without printing a value.
# Guest keys only: never TUNNEL_TOKEN, ACCESS_*, radarr/sonarr/qbit/WUD/Kuma/Prowlarr keys, Discord webhooks,
# OWNER_EMAIL_*, ICS_URL_*, money keys, HUB_DEV or GUEST_DEV_OWNER (tests/deploy/test_joey_media_service.py).
# It is an env_file, read at container start: after a change run `docker compose up -d joey-media`, not a reload.
# Owner ids are resolved once per process (WP-A2): after a new JELLYFIN_USER_ALIASES entry or friend user, restart
# BOTH: `docker compose up -d hub joey-media`.
JELLYFIN_URL=
JELLYFIN_API_KEY=
JELLYFIN_USER=
JELLYFIN_USER_ALIASES=
# JELLYFIN_USER_HER=   (unset on the NAS, Q16)
JELLYSEERR_URL=
JELLYSEERR_API_KEY=
OMDB_API_KEY=
JELLYFIN_PUBLIC_URL=https://jellyfin.joeyhome.net:8443
